## **SUGESTÕES DE CORREÇÃO**

### **1. Eliminar Polling - MessageQueue Consumer:**
```cpp
// ❌ INCORRETO (polling):
while (messages_processed.load() < 1000) {
    if (queue.try_dequeue(msg)) {
        // process
    } else {
        std::this_thread::sleep_for(std::chrono::microseconds{10}); // POLLING!
    }
}

// ✅ CORRETO (event-driven):
void consumer_async(MessageQueue& queue, std::promise<void> completion) {
    queue.async_dequeue([&](QueuedMessage msg) {
        // Process message
        if (messages_processed.fetch_add(1) >= 1000) {
            completion.set_value();
        } else {
            consumer_async(queue, std::move(completion)); // Continue async
        }
    });
}
```

### **2. Threading Context sem Busy-Wait:**
```cpp
// ❌ INCORRETO:
while (io_tasks_completed.load() < kNumIoTasks || 
       cpu_tasks_completed.load() < kNumCpuTasks) {
    std::this_thread::sleep_for(std::chrono::milliseconds{10});
}

// ✅ CORRETO (promise-based):
void demonstrate_threading_context() {
    ThreadingContext threading{1, std::thread::hardware_concurrency()};
    
    std::promise<void> io_completion;
    std::promise<void> cpu_completion;
    auto io_future = io_completion.get_future();
    auto cpu_future = cpu_completion.get_future();
    
    std::atomic<int> io_completed{0}, cpu_completed{0};
    
    // Submit tasks with completion signaling
    for (int i = 0; i < kNumIoTasks; ++i) {
        threading.post_io([&]() {
            // Work here
            if (io_completed.fetch_add(1) + 1 == kNumIoTasks) {
                io_completion.set_value();
            }
        });
    }
    
    // Wait properly without polling
    io_future.wait();
    cpu_future.wait();
}
```

