## SUGESTOES DE CORRECAO

**1. Correção do destructor (fire-and-forget)**
```cpp
~ContextGuard() {
    try {
        if (!context_id_.empty() && client_) {
            // Force terminal to ensure operation executes
            auto close_task = client_->close_context(context_id_);
            close_task.finally([](auto&&...) { 
                // Fire-and-forget cleanup
            });
        }
    } catch (...) {
        // Ignore cleanup errors in destructor
    }
}
```

**2. Melhor ainda - operação síncrona no destructor**
```cpp
~ContextGuard() {
    try {
        if (!context_id_.empty() && client_) {
            // Use sync version for deterministic cleanup
            auto close_task = client_->close_context(context_id_);
            close_task.sync(); // or .get() if available
        }
    } catch (...) {
        // Ignore cleanup errors in destructor
    }
}
```

**3. Construtor com validação**
```cpp
ContextGuard(std::shared_ptr<Client> client, std::string context_id)
    : client_{std::move(client)}, context_id_{std::move(context_id)} {
    if (!client_) {
        throw std::invalid_argument("Client cannot be null");
    }
    if (context_id_.empty()) {
        throw std::invalid_argument("Context ID cannot be empty");
    }
}
```

**4. Move assignment corrigido**
```cpp
ContextGuard &operator=(ContextGuard &&other) noexcept {
    if (this != &other) {
        // Clean up current state first
        context_id_.clear();
        
        client_ = std::move(other.client_);
        context_id_ = std::move(other.context_id_);
        other.context_id_.clear();
    }
    return *this;
}
```

